clark county coroner has now identified  at least two of the victims from  sunday's deadly plane crash in north las  vegas 82 year old donald stewart  goldberg and 76 year old carol ann  scanlan died sunday after two planes  collided in midair now we are still  waiting on the ids of the other two  people that were killed but family  members have identified another 47 year  old zach rainey he was on board with his  flight instructor victoria saha spoke  with rainey's family as they cope with  their enormous  grief as people driving by glance at  what's left of one of the planes  involved in sunday's crash there's a hat  here left by friends and family of zach  rainey as a reminder of a man who was  looking forward to getting his pilot's  license it's been more than 48 hours  since tara tidwell spoke to zach rainey  on what would be their last conversation  forever i was actually speaking with him  on the phone when he pulled up to flight  school  it was about 10 45 a.m and we were  discussing our plans to go to the ball  game rainey and tidwell were married for  14 years and share two young sons  tidwell describes rainey as a free  spirit a man who loved to give and  someone who couldn't wait to fly he was  really close to being done and being  able to fly on his own and he was  definitely having conversations with his  kids about taking them up and his  friends on sunday's class was supposed  to be one step closer to making his  dreams come true zach was afraid of  anything  he was fearless rainey was on board the  cessna with his instructor from airwork  las vegas a flight school near the north  las vegas airport when it collided with  a piper malibu coming in from idaho i  texted him and he didn't text me back  i got worried  i looked up the video and the news i  came by i found his car at the flight  school  so i knew  it was about the same time i got the  call from the coroner the piper malibu  was flown by 82 year old donald goldberg  his passenger 76 year old 